# JavaScript File Structure

## Core rules

1. **Max 500 lines** per `.js` file.
2. **One page entry:** `js/pages/{pageName}/index.js` — wire-up only; no large logic.
3. **Split by purpose:** `state/`, `parse/`, `render/`, `export/`, `ui/`, `utils/`, `loaders/` as needed.
4. Only create folders that match real responsibilities.

## Layout

```
js/
  components/          ← shared (pageShell, etc.)
  pages/{pageName}/
    index.js           ← HTML imports this only
    state|render|ui|utils|loaders/
  portal/              ← legacy feature bundles until migrated
```

HTML lives under `pages/{pageName}/`. Portal feature code may stay in `js/portal/` until migrated.

## `index.js` should

- Import modules, register init, attach listeners, call setup exports

## `index.js` must not

- Hold large parse/render/export implementations
- Exceed 500 lines
- Duplicate supporting-file logic

## HTML import

```html
<script type="module" src="../../js/pages/{pageName}/index.js"></script>
```

Use ES modules (no build step). camelCase filenames by purpose.

## When to split

Split near 500 lines, multiple responsibilities, or reusable/testable slices. Keep tiny related helpers together.

## Checklist

- [ ] Single `index.js` script tag on the page
- [ ] Entry + supporting files each under 500 lines
- [ ] Folders by purpose; ES `import`/`export`
